# Logitech G305 (046d:4074, paired to a 046d:c53f receiver) -> uaccess on its
# own hidraw node.
#
# Matched the same way as the G502 X PLUS's wireless rule, and for the same
# reason: this receiver gives a paired device a hidraw node of its own, so the
# device can be named directly instead of granting the receiver's interfaces,
# which carry the traffic of everything paired to it.
#
# Pair nothing else to this mouse's receiver, for the reason 70-g502x.rules
# gives. The G305 connects over eQUAD Lightspeed 1.1, a link hid-logitech-dj
# marks as taking keyboard reports, and the driver hands each keyboard report
# to the first such device in slot order. With a keyboard paired after the
# mouse, its keystrokes would arrive on this node, the one this file grants.
# Read from the driver, not checked on hardware.
#
# Read off the hardware on 2026-09-22: the receiver presents interfaces 00,
# 01 and 02, and the G305 appears as a separate node with no interface of its
# own. KERNELS matches a parent's kernel name, which for the paired device is
# bus:vendor:product.instance -> 0003:046D:4074.<n>.
KERNEL=="hidraw*", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", KERNELS=="0003:046D:4074.*", TAG+="uaccess"
